1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
In February 2022, Kanye West publicly objected to his daughter being on TikTok.

2
00:00:06,269 --> 00:00:11,060
Three years later, he released a song featuring that same daughter and Sean Combs.

3
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:13,650
Despite Kim Kardashian's attempt to stop it.

4
00:00:14,699 --> 00:00:19,129
Somewhere between those two decisions, a disagreement about protecting North West

5
00:00:19,429 --> 00:00:22,250
Had become a fight over who controlled her public life.

6
00:00:23,230 --> 00:00:27,370
And by the summer of 2026, even a greeting at a fashion show.

7
00:00:27,699 --> 00:00:29,449
Was being pulled into the argument.

8
00:00:34,299 --> 00:00:37,229
At first glance, the story seems easy to explain.

9
00:00:37,899 --> 00:00:40,909
Kanye believes Kim is exposing their daughter to too much.

10
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:45,170
Kim believes Kanye's public attacks are making things worse.

11
00:00:46,159 --> 00:00:50,369
But follow what they actually did and that explanation starts to break down.

12
00:00:51,159 --> 00:00:57,000
Because when Kim tried to stop one particular release, Kanye was the person pushing it into the world.

13
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,219
To understand how they reached that point, we need to go back to a much smaller piece of content.

14
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:04,719
A TikTok video.

15
00:01:05,729 --> 00:01:10,989
In February 2022, Kanye objected publicly to North's TikTok presence.

16
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:17,640
Kim defended it as supervised creative activity and said his public attacks were causing harm.

17
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:22,620
The disagreement was already playing out through the platforms they were arguing about.

18
00:01:23,519 --> 00:01:28,450
Kanye could object to an audience watching his daughter, but once he made that objection public,

19
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:31,150
It gave that audience another reason to look.

20
00:01:32,079 --> 00:01:34,629
Now the content had a second story attached to it.

21
00:01:35,129 --> 00:01:36,969
A dispute between her parents.

22
00:01:37,969 --> 00:01:40,359
Kim's response offered a different explanation.

23
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:46,489
In her account, she was letting her daughter enjoy a creative outlet while an adult supervised.

24
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:51,659
She also said she wanted matters involving the children handled privately.

25
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:53,719
That was the divide.

26
00:01:54,469 --> 00:01:56,329
One parent challenged the exposure.

27
00:01:56,829 --> 00:01:58,959
The other challenged the way he was handling it.

28
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,680
Neither argument stayed between them.

29
00:02:02,379 --> 00:02:06,700
Later that February, the dispute appeared in reporting about their divorce proceedings.

30
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:12,449
According to The Guardian, Kim said in court documents that Kanye's social media posts

31
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:14,520
Had caused emotional distress.

32
00:02:15,379 --> 00:02:18,599
She wanted the marriage legally ended so she could move forward.

33
00:02:19,509 --> 00:02:21,490
This was her account in those documents.

34
00:02:22,050 --> 00:02:24,469
It did not settle every disagreement between them.

35
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:27,330
But it showed how far the conflict had traveled.

36
00:02:27,909 --> 00:02:31,349
From social media posts into the effort to end their marriage.

37
00:02:32,270 --> 00:02:35,569
The public had fragments. The parents had a disagreement.

38
00:02:36,229 --> 00:02:37,969
North had her name attached to both.

39
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:42,659
Then, in March 2025, the roles changed.

40
00:02:43,490 --> 00:02:47,509
Kanye released a track called Lonely Roads Still Go to Sunshine.

41
00:02:48,319 --> 00:02:50,509
It featured North and Sean Combs.

42
00:02:51,449 --> 00:02:57,330
People reported that Kim had tried to prevent its release, with the dispute involving the use of North's name.

43
00:02:58,310 --> 00:03:03,599
This time, Kim was the parent trying to keep a particular piece of content out of circulation.

44
00:03:04,349 --> 00:03:05,840
Kanye released it anyway.

45
00:03:06,639 --> 00:03:11,349
And the reported messages surrounding that release made the disagreement even more revealing.

46
00:03:12,379 --> 00:03:16,030
The Independent described screenshots Kanye was reported to have shared.

47
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:21,669
In that exchange, Kim said they had previously agreed to trademark their children's names

48
00:03:21,969 --> 00:03:23,659
To prevent other people using them.

49
00:03:24,599 --> 00:03:27,419
She said she had sent paperwork to keep North off the song.

50
00:03:28,439 --> 00:03:31,280
Kanye's reported response included eight words.

51
00:03:31,819 --> 00:03:33,819
Amend it or I'm going to war.

52
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:38,639
The same report described him warning about public fallout for both of them.

53
00:03:39,509 --> 00:03:43,990
These were reported messages, not a complete record of their private conversations.

54
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:47,039
But the dispute they described was specific.

55
00:03:47,849 --> 00:03:50,719
Kim was invoking a protection she said they had agreed on.

56
00:03:51,449 --> 00:03:53,270
Kanye was demanding a change.

57
00:03:54,099 --> 00:03:55,889
There were two things happening at once.

58
00:03:56,409 --> 00:03:59,120
A disagreement over whether North should appear on the track.

59
00:03:59,550 --> 00:04:02,840
And a disagreement over the mechanism Kim was using to object.

60
00:04:03,909 --> 00:04:06,280
The reported trademark exchange connected them.

61
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,479
Something Kim described as protection became something Kanye wanted changed.

62
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:13,770
Before the argument escalated further.

63
00:04:14,819 --> 00:04:19,610
For viewers following only the latest angry post, that background was easy to miss.

64
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:22,449
But it explains why the messages mattered.

65
00:04:23,410 --> 00:04:26,490
This was a dispute about a release that people could actually hear.

66
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:30,329
Involving a child whose parents were openly disagreeing about it.

67
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:36,839
That is a much harder episode to fit into the idea that Kanye was simply trying to keep North away from publicity.

68
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:40,550
He was actively choosing a public project for her.

69
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:43,879
When Kim objected, the project went ahead.

70
00:04:44,829 --> 00:04:47,290
It does not tell us everything about his intentions.

71
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:50,949
It does tell us that his objections to exposure had limits.

72
00:04:51,709 --> 00:04:55,129
Apparently, being the parent behind the release made a difference.

73
00:04:56,079 --> 00:04:58,079
The conflict continued beyond that song.

74
00:04:58,870 --> 00:05:03,540
Reporting days later described Kanye objecting to a proposed musical collaboration.

75
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:05,769
Involving Playboi Carti and North.

76
00:05:06,769 --> 00:05:09,329
He accused Kim of encouraging it without his consent.

77
00:05:09,769 --> 00:05:13,100
And complained about control over the children's creative involvement.

78
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,990
Set those episodes beside each other.

79
00:05:16,810 --> 00:05:20,480
Kim objected to one project, Kanye objected to another.

80
00:05:21,410 --> 00:05:26,930
Both disputes involved North's music and both became public arguments about parental authority.

81
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:30,529
Supporting her creativity was something they could each claim.

82
00:05:31,339 --> 00:05:33,779
Agreeing on who could approve it was another matter.

83
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:39,170
By then, the question had moved well beyond whether a child should appear in a TikTok.

84
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:42,629
It involved music releases, the use of a name,

85
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:45,949
And opportunities that could become part of a public career.

86
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,129
The song and the proposed collaboration also exposed a practical problem.

87
00:05:52,009 --> 00:05:56,589
If both parents support a musical future but disagree over individual projects,

88
00:05:57,069 --> 00:05:59,840
Every new opportunity can reopen the same dispute.

89
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:03,090
The audience may see separate controversies.

90
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:07,930
Underneath them is an unresolved question about how decisions get made.

91
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:13,480
And whether either parent can object without that objection becoming another public confrontation.

92
00:06:14,810 --> 00:06:20,310
And in June 2026 a completely different moment brought North back into the headlines.

93
00:06:21,209 --> 00:06:26,500
Page Six reported on her greeting with adult model an adult model at a Paris fashion event.

94
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:28,519
She offered a handshake.

95
00:06:29,110 --> 00:06:30,550
He responded with an embrace.

96
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,490
Skepta criticized the interaction.

97
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:37,629
While a source quoted in the report disputed that North had been uncomfortable.

98
00:06:38,579 --> 00:06:43,699
What the report established was a public greeting and disagreement over how to interpret it.

99
00:06:44,490 --> 00:06:46,899
It did not establish a romantic relationship.

100
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,040
That distinction matters to the story.

101
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,259
Turn the greeting into a claim about dating.

102
00:06:53,649 --> 00:06:57,149
And the entire argument rests on something the evidence does not show.

103
00:06:58,050 --> 00:07:01,029
There is already enough to examine without adding that claim.

104
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:06,629
North's public appearances had become another place where people could debate her parents.

105
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:11,420
A brief interaction could be treated as evidence about years of parenting.

106
00:07:12,050 --> 00:07:14,459
Even though the clip could not provide that history.

107
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:19,180
Then, in August, North offered a glimpse of her own perspective.

108
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:24,459
People's coverage of her Dazed interview described her as uninterested in dating.

109
00:07:24,870 --> 00:07:27,540
And focused instead on her style and interests.

110
00:07:28,519 --> 00:07:33,500
Separate coverage of the interview reported that she wanted an ordinary job at Starbucks when she was older.

111
00:07:34,509 --> 00:07:37,930
Those comments were a reminder that the person at the center of this story

112
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,740
Had interests beyond her parents' disagreements.

113
00:07:41,659 --> 00:07:44,449
They also complicated the assumptions being made about her.

114
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:47,830
The public could build a narrative from an appearance.

115
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:51,710
North could say something quite different about what she actually wanted.

116
00:07:52,629 --> 00:07:55,629
None of that answers every question about Kim's decisions.

117
00:07:56,810 --> 00:08:00,860
Her explanation has been that she supports creative expression with supervision.

118
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:07,659
But supervising the making of a video does not give a parent control over every reaction after it is published.

119
00:08:08,689 --> 00:08:11,069
That is the gap her explanation leaves open.

120
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:14,019
How much public exposure is appropriate.

121
00:08:14,639 --> 00:08:16,139
Which opportunities should wait?

122
00:08:17,110 --> 00:08:20,230
Where does a parent's responsibility to set a limit come in?

123
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:24,639
Those questions apply even when a child enjoys performing.

124
00:08:25,610 --> 00:08:29,460
Enjoyment is part of the decision. It cannot be the whole decision.

125
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:33,440
Kanye meanwhile has another problem to account for.

126
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:38,990
His criticism of exposure sits alongside his own decision to release North's work.

127
00:08:39,379 --> 00:08:40,899
Over an objection from her mother.

128
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:45,620
A concern can be reasonable while the response to it makes things worse.

129
00:08:46,539 --> 00:08:49,180
Taking the disagreement online adds an audience.

130
00:08:49,690 --> 00:08:53,039
But that audience cannot negotiate the next parenting decision.

131
00:08:53,889 --> 00:08:56,059
It can only react to the version it sees.

132
00:08:57,120 --> 00:09:01,220
And the song dispute shows why choosing a side too quickly misses the point.

133
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:05,529
Kim was resisting a release. Kanye was advancing it.

134
00:09:06,389 --> 00:09:11,159
The familiar story about which parent wanted publicity did not explain that episode.

135
00:09:12,129 --> 00:09:16,100
This does not prove they bear equal responsibility for everything that has happened.

136
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:18,559
The reporting cannot tell us that.

137
00:09:19,470 --> 00:09:24,789
It gives us specific decisions to judge and those decisions do not support a simple account.

138
00:09:25,090 --> 00:09:29,019
In which one parent always protects and the other always exposes.

139
00:09:30,169 --> 00:09:32,659
The TikTok argument was about a public platform.

140
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,610
The song dispute was about a public release.

141
00:09:36,509 --> 00:09:39,279
The Paris controversy grew around a public appearance.

142
00:09:40,149 --> 00:09:45,480
Across all three, North's name kept becoming the place where adults argued about boundaries.

143
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:48,529
Kanye can question Kim's judgment.

144
00:09:49,139 --> 00:09:50,720
Kim can question his conduct.

145
00:09:51,539 --> 00:09:53,950
But their own choices remain part of the record.

146
00:09:54,610 --> 00:09:56,970
Including the moments when their positions reverse.

147
00:09:58,019 --> 00:10:03,440
The next time one of these arguments produces another post, another screenshot, or another headline,

148
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:05,569
That is the part worth remembering.

149
00:10:06,750 --> 00:10:11,059
Winning the argument online has never been the same thing as resolving it at home.
